  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Milburn’s absurdly ambitious report offers blueprint for fixing everything and everyone",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2026/nov/17/alan-milburn-neet-report-absurdly-ambitious-analysis",
      "description": "<p>He lays out sweeping aims and finer details for how to fix the Neets crisis – and is obsessive about welfare</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/society/2026/nov/17/neet-alan-milburn-report-young-people-not-in-education-employment-or-training\">Neet ideas: what’s in Milburn’s report?</a></p></li></ul><p>It is not clear if too many people were expecting Everything Everywhere All at Once, but that is what Alan Milburn has delivered. <a href=\"https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/from-a-welfare-state-to-a-working-state-a-new-settlement-for-the-next-generation\">From a Welfare State to a Working State </a>is almost absurdly ambitious. The <a href=\"https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/terms-of-reference-for-the-independent-report-into-young-people-and-work/terms-of-reference-report-into-young-people-and-work\">terms of reference</a> said something about the drivers of youth labour markets. We got a blueprint for how to fix everything and everyone.</p><p>What Keir Starmer, who commissioned it, had in mind, we’ll never know, but Milburn has taken up with gusto Andy Burnham’s general invocation to think boldly and rewire the state. Yes, it’s about training and jobs, but it’s also about pulling apart the NHS, giving schools and colleges an MOT, and once again, <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/society/2026/nov/17/alan-milburn-report-young-people-work-neets-job-support-savingsalan-milburn-plan-young-people-work-neets-savings-200m-a-year\">blowing up old-fashioned social security</a>.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/society/2026/nov/17/alan-milburn-neet-report-absurdly-ambitious-analysis\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-17T19:47:31"
    },
    {
      "title": "Milburn calls for tax cuts for businesses hiring young people despite union concerns",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2026/nov/17/alan-milburn-tax-cuts-businesses-unions-neets-youth-unemployment",
      "description": "<p>Youth unemployment review risks clash with unions and Labour left over workers’ rights and minimum wage</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/society/2026/nov/17/neet-alan-milburn-report-young-people-not-in-education-employment-or-training\">Neet ideas: what’s in Alan Milburn’s youth unemployment report?</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/society/2026/nov/17/who-are-neets-uk-youth-job-crisis-charts\">Who are the Neets? UK youth job crisis in five charts</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/society/2026/nov/16/alan-milburn-urges-burnham-spend-billions-new-deal-young-people-youth-jobs-crisis-welfare-employment\">Milburn urges Burnham to spend billions on young people</a></p></li></ul><p>Alan Milburn has called on ministers to cut business taxes and ease regulations to encourage employers to hire more young people, setting up a potential clash with trade unions and the Labour left over employment rights.</p><p>The former health secretary published the results of his year-long review into youth unemployment on Wednesday, in what the prime minister, Andy Burnham, called a “watershed moment” for young people.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/society/2026/nov/17/alan-milburn-tax-cuts-businesses-unions-neets-youth-unemployment\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-17T19:30:32"
    },
    {
      "title": "Burnham delays announcement about options for closer relationship with EU until next month – as it happened",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/nov/17/alan-milburn-youth-unempolyment-neets-economy-welfare-brexit-latest-news-updates",
      "description": "<p>The prime minister earlier said he wanted to open a national debate on Britain’s relationship with the bloc</p><p>This chart, from the Milburn report, shows what is likely to happen to the Neet rate, with or without the Milburn policies.</p><p>The Alan Milburn report has now formally been published. It should be online <a href=\"https://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/department-for-work-pensions\">here</a> very soon.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/nov/17/alan-milburn-youth-unempolyment-neets-economy-welfare-brexit-latest-news-updates\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-17T17:46:07"
    }
